# mcp-tee env allowlist — wire-ipc plugin (wire-ipc 1.9.0 + @agiterra/wire-ipc-tools v2.7.1 + wire-tools v2.25.2).
# Base set (PATH HOME USER LOGNAME SHELL LANG LC_* TERM TMPDIR TZ) is implicit.
# ENG-5158. Built from a static read of server.ts + node_modules/@agiterra/*
# (tests excluded) on 2026-10-20. The server spawns no subprocesses.
# Reached directly: AGENT_ID AGENT_PRIVATE_KEY WIRE_URL (wire-ipc-tools startServer), STE_* (ste-lint), HOME.
# The rest are read only by wire-tools modules wire-ipc does not import today (mcp-server, sse-runner);
# kept so a wire-tools bump that starts importing them does not silently lose them. None is a secret.
AGENT_*                  # AGENT_ID AGENT_NAME AGENT_PLAN AGENT_PRIVATE_KEY (signing)
WIRE_*                   # WIRE_URL WIRE_MCP_INBOUND WIRE_SCREEN_NAME WIRE_SSH_HOST WIRE_RUN_AS_UID WIRE_HEALTH_INTERVAL_MS
STE_*                    # STE_GLOSSARY_PATH STE_RULES_PATH (ste-lint)
CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID   # session binding (wire-tools mcp-server)
STY                      # screen name self-report (deriveScreenName)
GROK_WIRE_BRIDGE         # inbound mode: =1 means a sidecar owns the stream
